55:**Sub-decision: how sign-off works.** (i) Drive the existing LangGraph review interrupt from the workspace. (ii) Make the case folder the source of truth, and make sign-off a case-log event bound to a snapshot hash. *Chose (ii)*. The figures are a pure function of the case's inputs, so a checkpoint would hold nothing extra, and re-running the graph after every override would also re-run the draft node. ReviewDecision's name and notes validation is reused, not copied. `cma run` keeps its interrupt unchanged. Revision 2 settles the order: the underwriter signs a preview, and the pack is written once, at sign-off, from that preview. Revision 1 said both that sign-off binds to a pack already built and that a pack is never overwritten, which left nowhere to record the sign-off.
89:- **C8 Verify** (new src/cma/verify.py). Recomputes an evidence record from its case and refuses records from another ruleset.
168:- **Platform.** *Blast radius:* one Python package; new optional parts; the evidence JSON gains fields; PolicyResult and the checkpoint allow-list do not change. *Old and new side by side:* `cma run` is untouched, new commands are additive, and CMA_RULESET=v1 reproduces today's categories, cash included. *Resources:* files on disk only; no tables, queues, cron jobs or IAM. *Rollback:* an environment flag (CMA_RULESET), a config flip (show_policy_verdict) or a reinstall, with no data repair. *Observability:* see that section.
216:**Policy check.** PolicyResult and policy.evaluate do not change. The workspace and the pack evaluate only the packaged policy. The label is one constant with no digits in it, so it never trips the guard: 'Illustrative thresholds shipped with this tool. They are not your firm's lending policy, and this is not a lending decision: the underwriter decides.' The pack's evidence records whether the check was shown, the label, and the policy's name and hash. These do not go into PolicyResult, so the checkpoint allow-list and `cma run` are untouched. As in revision 1, the description of policy rule R9 is reworded for M16's new name, and the policy hash changes.
238:**Evidence JSON v1.** Everything in today's record, with its policy key unchanged. Added: schema_version, case id, accounts (key, source format, file hash, period, line count), ruleset id and hash, firm rules hash, thresholds hash, profile hash, overrides (sequence number, line, old and new category, reason, name, OS user, time), money-in buckets, monthly summary, indicators with the thresholds that fired, policy_check (shown or hidden, the label, the policy name and hash), snapshot hash, sign-off (name, OS user, time, notes), egress (offline, or the model's name) and package version.
307:| An evidence record was made with a different ruleset | Verify refuses and names the version that made it | R45 |
318:- Pending reviews in a --checkpoint-db written by the old version still resume: the new Transaction fields have defaults, no Category value is removed, and PolicyResult does not change. No new type travels through the graph state, so CHECKPOINT_TYPES does not change.
337:**Rollback.** For the policy check, set show_policy_verdict off. For categorisation, cash included, set CMA_RULESET=v1 or reinstall the previous wheel. Packs and evidence are immutable and record their ruleset, thresholds, policy hash, the show_policy_verdict setting and package version, so nothing needs repair. The old version leaves case folders written by the new one alone.
